  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nuku&#x2019;alofa Port Upgrade &#x2013; Tonga &#x2013; Transport</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia provided a grant package for Government of  Kingdom of Tonga alongside support from Asian Development Bank to upgrade to Queen Salote International Wharf of Nuku&#x2019;alofa Port. Works include rehabilitating existing port infrastructure across four wharves &amp; expanding shipping capabilities to facilitate increased international operations.  Project&#x2019;s climate-resilience measures include building a concrete seawall &amp; strengthening existing rock walls to protect against sea level rise; upgrading port access roads; installation of solar powered lighting; upgrading rainwater harvesting systems; &amp; improving stormwater drainage. In emergencies,  upgrades enable Tonga to continue trading &amp; quickly deploy lifesaving products and services to communities. The project includes institutional strengthening support for Ports Authority of Tonga to improve operational practices, develop an asset maintenance plan &amp;  training on port operations, environmental sustainability, health/safety &amp; security.</narrative>
  </description>
