  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening leadership</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024, the upgrade of Tonga&#x2019;s international maritime port&#x2014;supported by a grant from the Australian Infrastructure Financing Facility for the Pacific (AIFFP)&#x2014;delivered significant local employment and skills development outcomes. 
&#x200d;
At the heart of the project were 137 Tongan workers, who made up an average of 77 per cent of the total workforce throughout the year. This far exceeded the original target of 20 per cent, reflecting a strong commitment to local participation. 
&#x200d;
Women also made their mark, with female workforce participation rising to 11 per cent over the life of the project in 2024, slightly above the 10 per cent target. Local media celebrated this shift, reporting a broader rise in women entering construction-related fields such as engineering, carpentry, and materials testing. 
&#x200d;
The project also supported on-the-job training for eight recent graduates&#x2014;four men and four women&#x2014;who were mentored by experienced engineers. Their training included practical exposure to interpreting technical drawings, using Computer Aided Design tools, conducting surveys, and managing Quality Assurance documentation. They also received targeted Health, Safety and Environment training, including working in confined spaces and at heights.</narrative>
    </description>
